{%- set faqs = [
  ["What cybersecurity services does CipherTrivia offer?", "CipherTrivia offers cybersecurity services including Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing (VAPT), web application security testing, API security assessments, cloud security reviews, infrastructure security assessments and AI-assisted security analysis. These services help businesses identify vulnerabilities, evaluate potential risks and prioritize security improvements."],
  ["What is Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing (VAPT)?", "Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing (VAPT) helps organizations identify security weaknesses and understand how attackers could exploit them. A vulnerability assessment identifies potential security gaps, while penetration testing evaluates the practical impact of selected vulnerabilities within an authorized testing scope."],
  ["Why does my business need a cybersecurity assessment?", "A cybersecurity assessment helps identify weaknesses in business applications, APIs, cloud environments and IT infrastructure before they lead to data exposure or operational disruption. It also helps businesses prioritize security investments, protect sensitive information and make informed decisions about risk reduction."],
  ["How does AI improve cybersecurity?", "Artificial intelligence can help security teams analyze application code, system configurations and technical data to identify suspicious patterns and potential vulnerabilities. When combined with expert validation, AI-assisted cybersecurity can improve analysis efficiency, help prioritize threats and reduce the effort required to investigate irrelevant findings."],
  ["What is the difference between vulnerability assessment and penetration testing?", "A vulnerability assessment focuses on identifying and evaluating security weaknesses across a defined environment. Penetration testing goes further by attempting to exploit selected vulnerabilities within an authorized scope to determine their potential impact. Both approaches help organizations understand security risks and plan corrective actions."],
  ["Which industries can benefit from CipherTrivia's cybersecurity services?", "CipherTrivia's cybersecurity services can support SaaS and technology companies, banking and fintech organizations, healthcare providers, ecommerce businesses, manufacturers, logistics companies, startups and enterprises. Each assessment can focus on industry-specific risks involving applications, sensitive data, connected systems and digital infrastructure."],
  ["Can CipherTrivia assess websites, APIs and cloud infrastructure?", "Yes. CipherTrivia can assess web applications, APIs, cloud environments and IT infrastructure based on the agreed scope of work. Security testing can identify access control weaknesses, insecure configurations, exposed services and other vulnerabilities that may affect business information or operations."],
  ["What happens after cybersecurity vulnerabilities are identified?", "After an assessment, the findings can be documented in a structured security report with severity ratings, supporting evidence and recommended remediation steps. Development and IT teams can use these findings to prioritize fixes, while follow-up testing can help verify that reported vulnerabilities have been addressed."],
  ["How long does a cybersecurity assessment take?", "The duration of a cybersecurity assessment depends on the size and complexity of the environment, the number of applications or systems being tested and the required testing depth. CipherTrivia can provide an estimated timeline after reviewing your business requirements and the proposed assessment scope."],
  ["How can I get started with CipherTrivia?", "Contact CipherTrivia to discuss your cybersecurity requirements, the systems you want to assess and your primary security concerns. Our team can help define an appropriate assessment scope and explain the proposed testing approach, deliverables and next steps."]
] %}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
